# UCSC's bigGenePredToGenePred, which fetch-genome.sh needs to build hs1's
# refGene.txt. Nothing else uses it.
#
# setup-mipgen.sh sources this file. deployment/docker/mipgen.Dockerfile names
# the same URL and hash in its BIGGENEPRED_* build arguments: update all three
# lines together.
#
# Why a pinned hash, and what happens when it goes stale: UCSC publishes no
# checksum file for its binaries, so TLS alone would mean installing whatever
# hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu serves that day and running it. With the hash, a
# changed file is refused. UCSC does replace this binary in place with every
# release, so the pin does go stale; when it does, the installers leave the
# tool out (and keep a copy that is already installed), say so, and carry on.
# Only hs1 is affected. To take the new file, check it yourself and give its
# hash for one run:
#
#   BIGGENEPRED_SHA256=<sha256 you checked> ./setup-mipgen.sh
#   docker compose build --build-arg BIGGENEPRED_SHA256=<sha256 you checked>
#
# then update the hash here.
#
# ⚠️ An empty hash means "not verified yet" and is refused like a wrong one.
# To fill it in, on any machine:
#
#   curl -fsSL --proto '=https' "$BIGGENEPRED_URL" | sha256sum
#
# Plain KEY=value lines only: this file is sourced by sh, not just bash.
BIGGENEPRED_URL=https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/admin/exe/linux.x86_64/bigGenePredToGenePred
BIGGENEPRED_SHA256=
